amming or judgment.","date":"","content":"\nVelocity-based training (VBT) uses the speed of a repetition—usually the concentric phase—to inform load selection, set termination, or readiness. It can make an important part of training more obser","category":"General"},{"slug":"wave-loading-hypertrophy-practical-guide","title":"Wave Loading for Hypertrophy: A Flexible Periodization Option","excerpt":"Wave loading varies training stress across sessions or weeks. It can organise progression, but it is not proven superior to simpler programmes for muscle growth.","date":"","content":"Wave loading varies a training variable—often load, repetitions, or volume—across a repeating pattern. A lifter might use a heavier session, a moderate session, and a higher-repetition session rather ","category":"General"},{"slug":"muscle-building-non-responders-science","title":"When Muscle Growth Seems Stalled: Measurement, Training, and Individual Response","excerpt":"Apparent non-response to hypertrophy training can reflect measurement noise, insufficient stimulus, nutrition, recovery, or genuine variation. Use a structured troubleshooting process before blaming genetics.","date":"","content":"\n\n“Non-responder” is an appealing label, but it is often applied too early. A short training block, one circumference measurement, changing technique, inconsistent food intake, or normal measurement e","category":"General"},{"slug":"mechanical-tension-vs-muscle-damage-growth","title":"Why Mechanical Tension, Not Muscle Damage, Drives Growth: The Science","excerpt":"Why muscle damage and soreness are not reliable growth targets, how mechanical loading fits the current hypertrophy model, and what to do in training.","date":"","content":"For decades, the fitness industry has pushed the idea that you need to \"destroy\" your muscles to grow them. The thinking goes: damage → repair → bigger muscle. But modern research tells a different st","category":"General"},{"slug":"effective-training-volume-quality-not-quantity","title":"Why Not All Sets Are Equal: The Science of Effective Training Volume","excerpt":"How set quality, proximity to failure, weekly volume, and recovery interact—and why there is no universal number of ‘effective’ sets for every lifter.","date":"","content":"If you track anything in the gym, it is probably sets and reps. You might also log load, rest, effort, and frequency. Those details are useful because a warm-up, a controlled work set, and a fatigued ","category":"General"},{"slug":"progress-stalled-hidden-factors-beyond-programming","title":"Why Progress Stalls: A Practical Audit Beyond Programming","excerpt":"Before changing your split, audit measurement, effort, recovery, nutrition, symptoms, and recent workload. A plateau needs evidence, not a random new stimulus.","date":"","content":"Progress rarely stops for one mysterious reason. A stalled lift or unchanged measurement can reflect a real plateau, normal noise, a missed progression target, poor recovery, an unhelpful exercise, or","category":"General"},{"slug":"women-men-muscle-building-2025-research","title":"Women and Muscle Building: What the Research Actually Shows","excerpt":"Women and men can both build substantial muscle with progressive resistance training; relative hypertrophy is similar in current evidence, while absolute outcomes and strength tests vary.","date":"","content":"\n\nWomen do not need a separate category of “toning” training, and men do not own the muscle-building playbook. Resistance training can increase muscle size and strength in both sexes. The useful quest","category":"General"},{"slug":"work-capacity-training-foundation-gains","title":"Work Capacity for Lifters: Build More Useful Training Tolerance","excerpt":"Work capacity is the ability to complete quality training and recover from it; build it gradually without confusing more fatigue or shorter rest with more muscle.","date":"","content":"\n\n“Work capacity” is often used loosely. For a lifter, it can mean completing more useful work at a given effort, recovering between sets, or tolerating a training week without performance collapsing.","category":"General"},{"slug":"zinc-muscle-building-testosterone-science","title":"Zinc, Training, and Testosterone: Food First, Claims Second","excerpt":"Zinc supports normal physiology, but supplementation helps testosterone or performance mainly when deficiency is present. Learn the food, safety, and testing boundaries.","date":"","content":"\n\nZinc is required for immune function, DNA and protein synthesis, growth, and normal reproductive physiology. That does not make it a general testosterone booster or a muscle-building shortcut.\n\n\n\nTr","category":"General"},{"slug":"zone-2-cardio-strength-athletes-gains","title":"Zone 2 Cardio for Lifters: Benefits, Tradeoffs, and Setup","excerpt":"Easy aerobic work can support health and conditioning, but its effect on strength and hypertrophy depends on dose, modality, scheduling, and recovery.","date":"","content":"“Cardio kills gains” is too simple, but so is “easy cardio never interferes.” Concurrent training research shows that resistance and endurance work can coexist. The result depends on how much work you","category":"General"}]